{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793526153,"nonce":"QSluFLGGGeWjgVzhqkmBYgNu8Co=","title":"kind: NetworkPolicy stops being enforced on a long-lived cluster (plugin isolation self-check fails)","message":"Seen 2026-11-01 in the AFK run 20261101-0058. On the kind cluster scarab-dev, 13 h old after many mode switches (dev/dogfood/e2e/chaos, Depot PVC deletes, toxiproxy apply/delete, ~hundreds of step Pods): the plugin-egress / default-deny NetworkPolicies in scarab-plugins existed and kindnet was Running and syncing nftables, yet a plugin Pod's isolation self-check reached the API server and the internet (lv-7-plugin-verify.log:40 'SCARAB_PROBE apiserver reached; SCARAB_PROBE internet reached'), and two scarab-plugin-k8s cluster tests failed (cluster.rs:500 self-check exit 1, cluster.rs:1030 writer Failed; lv-1-e2e.log). The same code on a FRESH cluster: just e2e 30/30 cluster tests and just plugin-verify PASSED (lv2-e2e.log, lv2-plugin-verify.log). The fix round between the two touched only image-load helpers, no network config.\nThe product behaved correctly: the plugin refused to start when its isolation self-check failed (fail-closed).\nWhy it matters: dogfood (staging) is meant to be long-lived; plugins would silently stop starting there, and any test relying on NetworkPolicy on an old cluster is unreliable.\nNext: reproduce (keep a cluster, churn modes, re-run just plugin-verify periodically), read kindnet's network-policy logs/nftables tables when it breaks, check kindnet version and known issues; possible mitigations: up.sh runs a cheap NetworkPolicy canary at start and refuses or recreates on failure; or pin a CNI with stable NetworkPolicy (e.g. Calico) for kind if the cost fits the ~2 GiB budget. Evidence dir: ~/.afk/scrarab-ci/20261101-0058/.","files":null}]}